Yeenoghu fhtagn!
A New Aeon of Horus as Anhur has begun!

Goodbye AniAhih the Demigod...
You and Aleister and Gabriel
went to your reward with 5576036 points,
Magicbane...
5 amulets of life saving [having used none...]
and 0 pieces of gold, after 133608 moves.
You were level 30 with a maximum of 1058 hit points when you ascended.

More stats after the story.

I decided beforehand to ascend with a tame untameable lich bearing the
name Aleister. (Uncle Al Crowley inspired my character.) At one point
I'd planned to tame one of each Nasty race, but I rejected this as
insane -- I wanted to genocide slimes and h, not cart them around with
me. And I decided that combining an arch-lich with a pet archon would
suffice to make AniAhih more powerful than Rodney. I also planned the
great Minetown Massacre from the start.

This game had an altar on level 3 along with a weapons shop, a sink and
the Mines entrance. Level 4 had a potions shop and another altar, not
to mention a magic trap and fountain. AniAhih must have received
Magicbane quickly. (Another altar appeared on level 12 along with the
Ludios portal.)

I don't recall if I did Sokoban or the Mines first. I do know that
Sokoban had the "oR, later encouraging me to create my first dragon
scale mail. A polymorph trap in the main dungeon produced a handy
silver dragon. I also know that a poly trap on Mines level 10 turned
Sif the cat into a tame green slime, since I no longer wanted one. I
let Sif go feral after that. At some point here, my wizard cleaned out
Fort Ludios and took the gold to the priest of Ptah in Minetown,
laughing fiendishly as he did so. Oh, and he must have tried on that
"oChange by mistake around this time.

Well-armed, my wizard proceeded to the lair of the Dark One. I hadn't
brought any scrolls of teleportation, but I did find one on the way. So
after checking the scroll's status at the Dark One's altar, I put on my
trusty =oTC and claimed the upstairs for myself. I had a bad moment
when the Dark One summoned a green slime right next to me, but Elbereth
took care of it -- no master mind flayers, thankfully -- and Magicbane
took care of the Dark One.

After freeing the prisoners and converting the altar, I went back to
explore the Home levels, finding a bag (ordinary sack) and elsewhere, a
polymorph trap next to a ring called regular geyser. "When life gives
you an amulet of change, make holy hand grenades," that's my motto. Now
seemed like a good time to signal the dawn of the New Aeon. AniAhih had
found the Dark One in a deserted temple of Ptah, and defeated him --
Anhur had succeeded where the slave-gods failed. It was time to begin
establishing his rule.

An old post of Dylan's told me how to avoid angering the Minetown
watch, and other posts added to my tactical plan. The priest of Ptah
gave me some trouble once I hit him with magic missile, refusing to
appear where I could hit him from outside. But half a dozen dead
insects later, a very kind rock mole ate most of the wall. Finger of
death! My friend the mole volunteered to increase the power of Anhur.
The priest left no corpse, so I couldn't sacrifice him on his own
converted altar, but some insects and a white unicorn (excellent
timing!) quickly supplied me with Frost Brand. I love Anhur. The holy
hand grenade goes back in the bag, until the next time paranoia seems
called for. I feared the priest would have a [CoMR, but my crowning
gift took his soul; and with my newly-uncursed robe, its failure rate
decreases from 43% to 3%!
(Note: at this point, I thought that sacrificing one's own race as a
chaotic on a cross-aligned altar would destroy the altar. This would
fit with the general rule of gods not accepting coracial sacrifice. It
would mean the deity of a non-chaotic altar will always "curse" the
altar, but tailors the curse to the offender. But I've since learned
that it doesn't work that way. YANI? Also, it seems unnecessary to
destroy a chaotic altar when the character has a different allegiance.
Why not just increase the alignment penalty so much that any
non-chaotic who gets a foocubus will probably have lost the power to
convert the altar?)

Somewhere in here I found a ?oI or 2, and identified rings of
protection from shape changers and slow digestion. I also had an
identified scroll of genocide. Back at my level 12 altar, I killed and
ate some mind flayers in the hope of getting 18 Int. After summoning
Juiblex, I decided to make some blessed potions of gain ability and
genocide h to protect my intelligence. Then I brought Juiblex to the
Mines and began the process of turning Minetown into Yeenoghu's Demonic
Orgy Town. I love Keystone Kops.

I went back to the 2 shops on altar levels of the main dungeon, and
summoned some more demons. (Remembering an "oLS I lost in a previous
game, I decided to go the ultra-paranoid route and wear my "oR whenever
not using my SDSM.) The potion shop supplied unholy water for cursing
my scroll of destroy armor, the better to fireproof my robe -- I'd
already fixed my speed boots. By now I had teleport control (at XP
level 17) and a =oSD, so I tried for teleportitis. "You feel in control
of yourself." When I did get jumpy, I found a bag of holding dropped by
a monster. With a ?oI inside, no less! My sacfest had given me a +oC,
though
a pyrolisk cost me some of my precious water and fruit juice -- I took
a potion and blessed the bag. Oh yes; AniAhih had just reached XPL 30
(Mage).

Having failed to do the math, I had some vague plan of getting another
"oChange and auto-cancelling every available foocubus after my
massacres. Well, I did wish for an "oCh at some point, since I had a
wish to burn, but I stopped the orgy at around 1000 HP. When I left the
Mines, Izchak the Illuminator ran a shop deep under the Earth in the
midst of a horde of demons, ruled by the Elder God of a vanished race.
The Faceless Lord Juiblex lurked just outside of town.

The rest of the game went according to plan. Well, I had to tame an
archon after wishing for his figurine, since he came into the game
peaceful. So much the better, it fit the original plan for surpassing
the WoY in magic. Also, I thought a pet demilich could grow into a
purple lich -- it worked that way back in my save-scumming days -- so I
tamed one between Medusa and the Castle only to have it die. The archon
Gabriel, on the other hand, stayed with his master from the Castle all
the way to the end. In fact, he helped to kill another archon, on one
of the Elemental Planes. I see here that I found two more temples in
the main dungeon, one co-aligned, plus another free-standing altar. The
vibrating square appeared at level 47. Upon reaching the Astral Plane,
AniAhih used his /oW to produce a tame arch-lich for ascension. He must
have found the right altar on the first try.

